    <bpmn:process id="W_W1849" name="W1849. Private Label Launch Campaign Planning &amp; Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New private label category ready for launch (products received at stores)
Frequency: ~2–4 category launches/year
Volume: Each launch covers 8–15 SKUs across 200 stores
Owner: CMO
Participants: CMO, Category Manager, VP Merchandising, Marketing Team, Store Operations
Source: workflow W1849 — Private Label Launch Campaign Planning &amp; Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1849_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1849_Lane1" name="CMO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1849_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1849_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1849_Lane2" name="Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1849_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1849_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1849_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1849_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1849_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1849_Start5" name="New private label category ready for launch (products received at stores)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1849_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1849_Task6" name="Pre-launch planning (4–6 weeks before launch): (a) CMO and Category Manager…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-launch planning (4–6 weeks before launch): (a) CMO and Category Manager define launch objectives: sales target, category penetration target, customer awareness target, (b) Marketing develops launch campaign: (i) in-store: product demonstration events, &quot;New at BuildRight&quot; signage, Sales Associate talking points, (ii) digital: social media posts (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok) showcasing product features, (iii) loyalty: double points on private label purchases for launch month, (iv) trade: direct communication to trade accounts with sample offer and introductory pricing, (c) budget allocation: marketing spend for launch (typically 2–3% of projected Year 1 category revenue)
Responsible (R): CMO / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1849_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1849_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1849_Task7" name="Sales Associate training (2 weeks before launch): (a) Marketing creates product…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sales Associate training (2 weeks before launch): (a) Marketing creates product training module: product features, quality story, price advantage vs. national brands, customer talking points, common questions and answers, (b) HR distributes training through Oracle Learning Management (OLA) per W51 (training), (c) Department Supervisors conduct brief team huddles on launch products in relevant departments
Responsible (R): Marketing / HR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1849_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1849_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1849_Task8" name="Launch week execution: (a) Marketing activates campaign: in-store signage…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Launch week execution: (a) Marketing activates campaign: in-store signage deployed, social media posts published, loyalty email/SMS sent to relevant customer segments, (b) Category Manager monitors real-time sales data: daily sales by SKU by store, (c) Store Operations ensures planogram compliance per W1848, (d) Sales Associates actively promote new products using talking points
Responsible (R): Marketing / Category Manager / Store Operations
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1849_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1849_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1849_Task9" name="Post-launch review (4 weeks after launch): (a) Category Manager and FP&amp;A…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-launch review (4 weeks after launch): (a) Category Manager and FP&amp;A analyze launch performance: actual sales vs. forecast, sell-through rate, margin performance, customer return rate, (b) CMO analyzes marketing effectiveness: campaign reach, conversion, cost per acquisition, (c) Category Manager decides: (i) if successful: continue standard merchandising; expand SKU range if demand supports, (ii) if below forecast: adjust marketing, pricing, or planogram placement; consider discontinuation if performance doesn&#x27;t improve within 3 months, (d) lessons learned documented for next launch
Responsible (R): Category Manager / CMO / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1849_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1849_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1849_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1849_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1849_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-366 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Brand, Packaging &amp; Marketing (PA-41.3).) | - operational: CMO review and approval gate
Owner: CMO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
