    <bpmn:process id="W_W1850" name="W1850. Private Label Customer Perception Survey &amp; Brand Health Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Semi-annual brand health survey; post-launch survey (3 months after category launch)
Frequency: Semi-annual comprehensive survey; post-launch pulse surveys
Volume: ~500–1,000 survey respondents per survey cycle (loyalty program members + trade account customers)
Owner: CMO
Participants: CMO, Market Research Analyst, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1850 — Private Label Customer Perception Survey &amp; Brand Health Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1850_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1850_Lane1" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1850_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1850_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1850_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1850_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1850_Lane2" name="CMO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1850_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1850_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1850_Start4" name="Semi-annual brand health survey; post-launch survey (3 months after category launch)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1850_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1850_Task5" name="Market Research Analyst designs survey instrument: (a) awareness: &quot;Have you…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Market Research Analyst designs survey instrument: (a) awareness: &quot;Have you noticed BuildRight&#x27;s own brand products in store?&quot;, (b) perception: &quot;How would you rate the quality of BuildRight Essentials/Pro products compared to national brands?&quot;, (c) purchase intent: &quot;Would you consider buying BuildRight brand for [category]?&quot;, (d) purchase behavior: &quot;Have you purchased BuildRight brand products? If yes, would you repurchase?&quot;, (e) price perception: &quot;Do you perceive BuildRight brand products as good value?&quot;, (f) improvement suggestions: &quot;What would make you more likely to buy BuildRight brand products?&quot;, (g) segment analysis: separate responses for DIY customers, trade professionals, and corporate buyers
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1850_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1850_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1850_Task6" name="Survey distribution: (a) email survey to loyalty program members (target…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Survey distribution: (a) email survey to loyalty program members (target: 500–800 responses), (b) SMS survey link to trade account customers (target: 100–200 responses), (c) in-store intercept survey at 10 stores during peak weekend (target: 100–200 responses), (d) survey incentive: 50 loyalty points for completion
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1850_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1850_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1850_Task7" name="Market Research Analyst analyzes results: (a) overall brand health score…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Market Research Analyst analyzes results: (a) overall brand health score (composite of awareness, perception, purchase intent, repurchase), (b) segment analysis: DIY vs. trade vs. corporate, (c) category-level analysis: which product categories have strongest private label acceptance?, (d) trend comparison: results vs. previous survey (improving/declining/stable), (e) verbatim analysis of open-ended responses for actionable insights
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1850_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1850_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1850_Task8" name="CMO presents brand health findings to VP Merchandising and Category Managers…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: CMO presents brand health findings to VP Merchandising and Category Managers: (a) actionable recommendations: product quality improvements, pricing adjustments, marketing message refinements, (b) category-specific actions: invest in categories with high acceptance; reevaluate categories with low acceptance, (c) competitive positioning: how does BuildRight private label perception compare to competitor private labels?
Responsible (R): CMO
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1850_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1850_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1850_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1850_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1850_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-366 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Brand, Packaging &amp; Marketing (PA-41.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: CMO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
