    <bpmn:process id="W_W1851" name="W1851. Private Label Competitor Benchmarking &amp; Market Positioning Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual competitive review; triggered by significant competitor private label launch or market shift
Frequency: Annual comprehensive review; ad-hoc for competitive threats
Volume: ~3–5 major competitors benchmarked (Wilcon Depot, CitiHardware, ACE Hardware, Handyman, local independents)
Owner: CMO
Participants: CMO, Market Research Analyst, Category Manager, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1851 — Private Label Competitor Benchmarking &amp; Market Positioning Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1851_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1851_Lane1" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1851_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1851_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1851_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1851_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1851_Lane3" name="CMO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1851_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1851_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1851_Start5" name="Annual competitive review; triggered by significant competitor private label launch or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1851_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1851_Task6" name="Market Research Analyst compiles competitor private label intelligence: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Market Research Analyst compiles competitor private label intelligence: (a) identify which competitors have private label programs, (b) catalog competitor private label product ranges: categories, SKU counts, brand names, (c) price benchmarking: competitor private label SRP vs. national brand SRP vs. BuildRight private label SRP (mystery shopping at 3–5 competitor stores per region), (d) quality assessment: purchase competitor private label products for side-by-side comparison with BuildRight and national brands, (e) packaging and branding comparison: design quality, shelf impact, labeling compliance, (f) in-store merchandising: planogram placement, signage, promotional support
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1851_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1851_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1851_Task7" name="Category Manager evaluates competitive positioning: (a) where does BuildRight…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager evaluates competitive positioning: (a) where does BuildRight have a private label advantage? (price, quality, range, merchandising), (b) where do competitors have an advantage? (c) are there product categories where competitors have private label but BuildRight does not? Should BuildRight enter? (d) are there categories where BuildRight should exit private label due to competitor dominance?
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1851_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1851_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1851_Task8" name="CMO and VP Merchandising review and decide on positioning adjustments: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CMO and VP Merchandising review and decide on positioning adjustments: (a) pricing adjustments if competitor private labels are significantly cheaper, (b) quality investment if competitor products are perceived as higher quality, (c) range expansion in underserved categories, (d) marketing message refinement to differentiate BuildRight&#x27;s private label story
Responsible (R): CMO / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1851_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1851_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1851_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1851_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1851_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-366 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Brand, Packaging &amp; Marketing (PA-41.3).) | - operational: CMO review and approval gate
Owner: CMO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
