    <bpmn:process id="W_W1853" name="W1853. Private Label Trade Marketing &amp; Contractor Program Integration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Private label launch targeting trade professionals; annual trade program review
Frequency: Per category launch targeting trade; annual program review
Volume: ~5,200 trade account customers; ~200 corporate account customers
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Manager, Account Manager, CMO
Source: workflow W1853 — Private Label Trade Marketing &amp; Contractor Program Integration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1853_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1853_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1853_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1853_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1853_Lane2" name="Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1853_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1853_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1853_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1853_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1853_Start5" name="Private label launch targeting trade professionals; annual trade program review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1853_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1853_Task6" name="For trade-targeted private label launches (e.g., &quot;BuildRight Pro&quot; fasteners…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For trade-targeted private label launches (e.g., &quot;BuildRight Pro&quot; fasteners, adhesives, PPE): (a) Category Manager defines trade pricing: quantity break tiers, trade account discount, project pricing for bulk orders, (b) Account Manager creates direct communication to top 500 trade accounts: product introduction, quality story, price advantage, sample offer (free sample pack of key SKUs for trial), (c) CMO develops trade-specific marketing: (i) trade flyer insert with private label products highlighted, (ii) contractor toolbox program — branded toolbox gift with minimum private label purchase, (iii) trade event presence: product samples at contractor networking events
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Account Manager / CMO
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1853_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1853_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1853_Task7" name="Trade account feedback collection: (a) Account Manager solicits feedback from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trade account feedback collection: (a) Account Manager solicits feedback from trade customers who tried private label products: quality assessment, willingness to continue using, price satisfaction, (b) Category Manager reviews feedback monthly: if quality concerns raised, escalate to QA Manager per W1839; if price concerns, evaluate pricing strategy per W1833
Responsible (R): Account Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1853_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1853_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1853_Task8" name="Annual trade program integration review: (a) VP Merchandising evaluates private…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual trade program integration review: (a) VP Merchandising evaluates private label penetration in trade account purchases: what % of trade account sales are private label? target: ≥ 15% within 2 years, (b) identify top trade accounts with zero private label adoption — Account Manager conducts targeted outreach, (c) evaluate if &quot;BuildRight Pro&quot; brand resonates with trade professionals or if repositioning needed
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 day/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1853_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1853_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1853_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1853_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
